  "question": "Background / Context\n\nThe project involves developing a mobile push notification system using Django. This system allows sending push notifications to mobile and web devices through multiple channels, including APNS (Apple Push Notification Service), FCM/GCM (Firebase Cloud Messaging/Google Cloud Messaging), WNS (Windows Notification Service), and WebPush. The system utilizes core Device models to manage and send notifications.\n\nObjectives\n\nThe primary objective is to enable efficient delivery of push notifications to a variety of devices. The system should facilitate sending both single and bulk notifications, handle device registrations, and update existing devices based on their registration IDs.\n\nStakeholders & Users\n\n- End Users: Individuals receiving notifications on their devices.\n- Administrators: Manage devices and notifications via the admin panel.\n- Developers: Implement and maintain the system within Django applications.\n\nFunctional Descriptions\n\n- Device Models: Implement models for different notification services (GCMDevice, APNSDevice, WNSDevice, WebPushDevice) with key attributes like name, active status, user linkage, device ID, and registration ID.\n- Notification Sending: Support sending notifications through various services either to individual devices or in bulk.\n- Admin Panel: Provide an interface to manage devices and facilitate testing of notifications, including a feature to handle duplicate registration IDs by updating existing records.\n\nNon-Functional Descriptions\n\n- Scalability: System must efficiently manage and send notifications to a potentially large number of devices.\n- Maintainability: Clean and adaptable code structure to allow easy updates and maintenance.\n- Performance: Ensure quick delivery of notifications with minimal delay for end users.\n- Security: Secure handling of user data and notifications, including proper management of user authentication and registration IDs.",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0030\nCREATE TABLE `device` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `active` tinyint(1) NOT NULL DEFAULT '1',\n  `user_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `device_id` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `registration_id` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `device_registration_id_uniq` (`registration_id`),\n  KEY `device_user_id_idx` (`user_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `device_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `auth_user` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `gcm_device` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `device_ptr_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `cloud_message_type` varchar(20) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `gcm_device_device_ptr_id_uniq` (`device_ptr_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `gcm_device_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`device_ptr_id`) REFERENCES `device` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `apns_device` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `device_ptr_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `certificate` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `application_id` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `apns_device_device_ptr_id_uniq` (`device_ptr_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `apns_device_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`device_ptr_id`) REFERENCES `device` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `wns_device` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `device_ptr_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `application_id` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `application_secret` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `wns_device_device_ptr_id_uniq` (`device_ptr_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `wns_device_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`device_ptr_id`) REFERENCES `device` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `webpush_device` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `device_ptr_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `auth` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `p256dh` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `webpush_device_device_ptr_id_uniq` (`device_ptr_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `webpush_device_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`device_ptr_id`) REFERENCES `device` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
